X-SOURCE-ID:localist_mccormicks_creek
SUMMARY:Fall Photo Contest\, McCormick's Creek State Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261101T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261101T120000
UID:30ffbc76372d353c8b2434a7f4275694@events.in.gov
DESCRIPTION:McCormick&rsquo\;s Creek Fall Photo Contest McCormick&#39\;s C
 reek seeks your help in gathering photos of the fall splendor at the park 
 by participating in our Fall Photo Contest.&nbsp\;The winning prize is a 2
 027 State Parks Annual Entrance Pass!&nbsp\;&nbsp\; To enter\, please send
  the following information in an email to &nbsp\; Jfiler@dnr.IN.gov &nbsp
 \;from Oct. 1\, 2026&ndash\;Nov. 14\, 2026 : Photo (attached as a jpeg\, j
 pg\, png) Participant name Address Date the photo was taken The winner wil
 l be selected by a panel of DNR staff\, and the entries will be shared on 
 the McCormick&rsquo\;s Creek Facebook page after the contest.&nbsp\; &nbsp
 \; Contest Rules: NO PURCHASE NECESSARY TO ENTER OR WIN. ALL FEDERAL\, STA
 TE\, LOCAL\, AND MUNICIPAL LAWS AND REGULATIONS APPLY. VOID WHERE PROHIBIT
 ED. 1. Eligibility: This contest is open to legal residents of the fifty (
 50) United States and the District of Columbia at the time of entry. Emplo
 yees of the Indiana Department of Resources and other companies associated
  with the promotion of this contest and their respective parents\, subsidi
 aries\, affiliates and advertising and promotion agencies as well as the i
 mmediate family (spouse\, parents\, siblings and children) and household m
 embers of each such employee are not eligible. 2. Sponsor: This contest is
  sponsored by the Indiana Department of Natural Resources (&ldquo\;Sponsor
 &rdquo\;). 3. All photos must have been created at McCormick&rsquo\;s Cree
 k State Park property.&nbsp\; 4. Agreement of Rules: Participation in this
  contest constitutes entrants full and unconditional agreement to and acce
 ptance of these rules and the decisions of the Sponsor\, which are final a
 nd binding. Winning a prize is contingent on being compliant with these ru
 les and fulfilling all other requirements set forth herein. 5. Contest Per
 iod: The contest begins on October 1\, 2026\, and the deadline to submit t
 he winter photo entries is 11:59 E.T. on November 14\, 2026. Entries that 
 are submitted before or after the contest period will be disqualified. Sub
 missions will be accepted for the duration of the contest using the online
  method only. 6. How to Enter: Online will be the only method of entry tha
 t is available\, it is available through&nbsp\;by email to&nbsp\; Jfiler@d
 nr.in.gov &nbsp\;and must follow the specific directions when filling out 
 the entry and submitting. All entries will become the property of the Spon
 sor and will not be returned. 7. Prize: Winner will be chosen by a panel o
 f Sponsor&rsquo\;s employees and will win a prize. The potential winner sh
 all be selected from all eligible entries received. The Sponsor will notif
 y the winner within two weeks of the end of the contest. If the potential 
 winner cannot be contacted within five (5) days after first contact the Sp
 onsor may select an alternate winner in his/her place from the remaining n
 on-winning\, eligible entries. The prize is: 2027 Annual Entrance Pass&nbs
 p\; 8. Winner Notification: Winners will be notified via email and announc
 ed via social media. 9. Release and Limitations of Liability: By participa
 ting in the contest\, entrants agree to release and hold harmless the Spon
 sor\, and each of their respective parents\, subsidiaries\, affiliates\, a
 dvertising and promotional agencies\, other companies associated with the 
 contest and each of their respective officers\, directors\, employees\, sh
 areholders\, representatives and agents from and against any claim or caus
 e of action arising out of the participation in this contest or receipt or
  use of prize. 10. Disputes: Except where prohibited\, each entrant agrees
  that any and all disputes\, claims and causes of action arising out of\, 
 or connected with\, the contest or any prize awarded shall be resolved ind
 ividually\, without resort to any form of class action\, and exclusively b
 y the appropriate court located in Indiana. 11. Privacy Policy: Informatio
 n collected from entrants is subject to Sponsor&rsquo\;s privacy policy. P
 hotos of the entered may be used in contest promotions and general communi
 cations\, including the DNR/State Park social media pages\, newsletters\, 
 and websites.
LOCATION:McCormick's Creek State Park\, 250 McCormick's Creek Park Road\, 
 Spencer\, IN 47460
URL:https://events.in.gov/event/fall-photo-contest-mccormicks-creek-state-
 park-3192
X-SOURCE:McCormick's Creek State Park
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Visit Bloomington": "https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/samuel-levi-jones-an-archaeology-of-knowledge/60099/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:visit_bloomington
SUMMARY:Samuel Levi Jones: An Archaeology of Knowledge
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261102
UID:d1445a82027f2d7efdd8581a1b8ed6d2@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:For more than a decade\, Indiana-born Samuel Levi Jones has cr
 eated abstract assemblages with found printed and bound matter\, deconstru
 cting encyclopedias\, law books\, medical texts\, and other didactic mater
 ials. Jones removes their fabric covers and pulps their pages\, sewing the
 se swatches together and applying paper pulp to create texturally rich\, c
 ollaged works with raw edges\, loose threads\, and worn surfaces. His proc
 ess of physically destroying archival materials and reconstructing them in
 to artworks constitutes a materially engaged critique of institutional aut
 hority\, reflecting on systems of knowledge that uphold power and privileg
 e in the United States. For his exhibition at the Eskenazi Museum\, Jones 
 mined the museum’s collection for works that resonate with the themes he
  interrogates\, including nationalism and patriotism\, censorship\, and th
 e representation marginalized identities in historical narratives. Borrowi
 ng its title from the ideas of the influential French philosopher Michel F
 oucault\, Samuel Levi Jones: An Archaeology of Knowledge comprises ten yea
 rs of Jones’ investigations into the underlying structures that shape ho
 w we see\, speak\, and think about culture\, politics\, and power.\nSuppor
 t for this exhibition has been generously provided by the Robert and Sara 
 LeBien Director's Endowment\, Charlie and Jeanetta Nelms\, and Janice L. W
 iggins.
GEO:39.1688819;-86.5198163
LOCATION:Eskenazi Museum of Art at Indiana University\, 1133 E. 7th Street
 \, Fine Arts Plaza\, Bloomington\, IN 47405
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/samuel-levi-jones-an-archaeolog
 y-of-knowledge/60099/
X-SOURCE:Visit Bloomington
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/events/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Visit Bloomington": "https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/the-photographic-reflex-the-lee-marks-and-john-c-deprez-jr-collection/60101/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:visit_bloomington
SUMMARY:The Photographic Reflex: The Lee Marks and John C. DePrez Jr. Coll
 ection
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261102
UID:cc83c1db2e79e0368cd16a8e10f10fde@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:Spanning more than 150 years\, The Photographic Reflex celebra
 tes a transformative gift to the Eskenazi Museum of Art at Indiana Univers
 ity: more than one hundred works by eighty artists\, generously donated by
  Lee Marks and John C. DePrez Jr. This exhibition features photographs dat
 ing from 1856 to 2017 and highlights the medium’s extraordinary range\, 
 both as a tool for documentation and as a vehicle for artistic exploration
 .\nFrom Alfred Stieglitz’s delicate studies of grass to Richard Misrach
 ’s vast images of the cosmos\, photographers have long found inspiration
  in the natural world. The built environment has also served as a compelli
 ng subject\, and the exhibition includes Berenice Abbott’s striking view
 s of 1920s New York City as well as Edward Burtynsky’s sweeping industri
 al landscapes.\nPhotography has played a central role in witnessing confli
 ct\, from Timothy H. O’Sullivan’s Civil War battlefield to iconic imag
 es from World War II\, Vietnam\, and beyond. While often associated with s
 traightforward depictions of reality\, photography also allows artists to 
 experiment with light\, exposure\, and process to construct imaginative sc
 enes and images beyond human sight.\nThe Photographic Reflex: The Lee Mark
 s and John C. DePrez Jr. Collection reveals photography’s power to refle
 ct and shape our perception of the world around us across time\, space\, a
 nd vision.\nLead support for this exhibition has been generously provided 
 by the Martha and David Moore Prints\, Drawings and Photographs Endowment
 \; Peter and Pamela DePrez\; Anne Marks Morgan\; Gregory Morse\; Efroymson
  Family Fund\; Anne N. DePrez\; John J. Medveckis\; and Friends of Lee Mar
 ks and John DePrez Jr.\nAdditional support provided by John M. (Jack) Reyn
 olds\, Jeffrey A. Wolin\, Sandi Clark\, and Katherine Campbell and Robert 
 J. Boeglin Jr.\, M.D.
GEO:39.1688819;-86.5198163
LOCATION:Eskenazi Museum of Art at Indiana University\, 1133 E. 7th Street
 \, Fine Arts Plaza\, Bloomington\, IN 47405
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/the-photographic-reflex-the-lee
 -marks-and-john-c-deprez-jr-collection/60101/
X-SOURCE:Visit Bloomington
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/events/
END:VEVENT
