 4868" data-max-w="250" data-max-h="125" loading="lazy" data-optimized="tru
 e"/></picture></td></tr><tr><td style="width: 99.9123%\;" colspan="2"><p s
 tyle="text-align: center\;">          &#160\;        </p><p style="text-al
 ign: center\;"><strong><em>Capturing the Campus: T.C. Steele\, Indiana Uni
 versity's First Artist in Residence</em></strong></p><p><em>Capturing the 
 Campus</em> pays tribute to renowned Hoosier artist T.C. Steele. The exhib
 it honors the century that has passed since his death by showcasing painti
 ngs form the artist's residency at IU and other relevant works. The exhibi
 t will bring together Steele's landscapes from the IU Public Art and Cultu
 ral Heritage Collection and the Indiana State Museum and Historic Sites' c
 ollection\, allowing the holdings of these two collections to be viewed in
  one space.        </p><p style="text-align: center\;"><strong>Dates: Apri
 l 17\, 2026 - April 2026</strong></p><p><picture class="lw_image lw_image3
