CATEGORIES:Lectures, talks, seminars, and conferences
DESCRIPTION:Today's 60-minute Virtual Information Session centers around t
 he Design-Build Studio\, an integral part of the Miller program curriculum
 . Faculty member Lucas Brown offers the presentation. The session will als
 o provide information on how to prepare your application. Bring your quest
 ions to the conversation.  The J. Irwin Miller Master of Architecture prog
 ram is a three-year in-residence program\, with a two-year advanced placem
 ent track possible for students who hold a B.Arch from a NAAB-accredited i
 nstitution or regional equivalent. With our twin studios approach\, studen
 ts take visual art course alongside architectural studios to develop their
  style of architectural design. The three-year program welcome applicants 
 from a variety of educational and career backgrounds.
LAST-MODIFIED:20261012T183203Z
LOCATION:Virtual
URL:https://events.iu.edu/soaadiub/event/2447903-miller-architecture-progr
 am-virtual-info-session-des
