BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Visit Bloomington": "https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/mary-oliver-saved-by-the-beauty-of-the-world-arthouse-now/59991/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:visit_bloomington
SUMMARY:Mary Oliver: Saved by the Beauty of the World | Arthouse Now
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261103T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261103T203000
UID:d7f6c240baed3c14ed98c824b6e2fdb8@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:Celebrated best-selling poet\, Pulitzer Prize-winner\, lover o
 f dogs and long walks in the woods\, openly queer but intensely private\, 
 Mary Oliver was America’s unlikely contemporary mystic\, stalking the po
 nds and forests of Cape Cod for nearly 50 years in order to open herself
 —and her readers—to the known and unknowable world. From a lonely chil
 dhood to literary fame\, Oliver’s life was shaped by devotion to nature
 \, paying attention\, and the long journey toward learning to love and to 
 be loved. Her poems inspire liberals and conservatives\, atheists and beli
 evers\, naturalists and urbanites\, speaking directly to contemporary anxi
 eties about attention\, presence\, and the human relationship with the nat
 ural world—issues that feel especially pressing in an era of climate cri
 sis\, digital distraction\, and social fragmentation. [91 min\; documentar
 y\; English]
GEO:39.168585;-86.517361
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 E. 7th Street\, Bloomington\, IN 47405
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/mary-oliver-saved-by-the-beauty
 -of-the-world-arthouse-now/59991/
X-SOURCE:Visit Bloomington
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/events/
END:VEVENT
