DESCRIPTION:November Theme: Paleontology Day: Thursdays Time: 10 - 10:30am
  Recommended Ages Children ages 2-6 and their caregivers Cost: Free for Me
 mbers / Free with Museum Admission Science Story Time is geared toward lis
 teners toddler through early elementary ages. This program uses children's
  picture books to engage as well as support scientific concepts and experi
 ments. Young scientists develop literacy and STEM skills as well as build 
 vocabulary by actively participating in the hands-on program. Activities d
 esigned for ages 3-6. All are welcome. Activities might include: Reading a
  story about how birds are dinosaurs and making a family tree together.
