BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"WFIU Community Calendar": "https://www.ipm.org/community-calendar/event/first-thursday-declaration-of-independence-lecture-13-10-2026-10-07-41"}
X-SOURCE-ID:wfiu_community_calendar
SUMMARY:First Thursday Declaration of Independence Lecture
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261105T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261105T235900
UID:86263212948023c48263b334004e9cfd@ipm.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims4/default/c881
 8ff/2147483647/strip/true/crop/250x250+0+0/resize/254x254!/quality/90/?url
 =http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Ffe%2Ff1%2Fef05cb5946238600
 19aa940c97ce%2F32759-lilly-nov-first-thurs-lw-square-avatar-rev-1790711261
 .jpg
DESCRIPTION:Presented by Lilly Library\nIU Libraries Lilly Library invites
  you to a special First Thursday talk in conjunction with our Declaration 
 of Independence exhibitions.\n As part of our yearlong America 250 program
 ming\, IU Associate Professor of History Konstantin Dierks will give a tal
 k entitled “Resonances of the Declaration of Independence in American Hi
 story.”\n Is it worth commemorating the Declaration of Independence in 2
 026? Does the Declaration still have resonance in our time of terrible cri
 sis? The Declaration expressed ideals with intensely contested and severel
 y limited meanings in 1776. Yet those brittle ideals somehow carried forwa
 rd through American history. Looking closely at the complexities of 1776 c
 an help us ponder how the Declaration might speak to our crisis in 2026.\n
  Before and after the talk\, please feel free to peruse our Declaration of
  Independence exhibitions: The Motives\, The Moment and The Signers.\nTick
 ets: https://events.iu.edu/libraries/event/first-thursday-declaration
LOCATION:Lilly Library\, 1200 E. 7th Street\, BLOOMINGTON\, Indiana 47405-
 3907
URL:https://www.ipm.org/community-calendar/event/first-thursday-declaratio
 n-of-independence-lecture-13-10-2026-10-07-41
X-SOURCE:WFIU Community Calendar
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.ipm.org/community-calendar/
END:VEVENT
