 1/src_region/0,0,640,427/10125_xxmarketing_websiteredesign_09262019_29_o4.
 rev.1639584487.jpg
CATEGORIES:Art and museum exhibitions,Culture and languages,Functions, fes
 tivals, and celebrations,Health and wellness
DESCRIPTION:Art can be anything that inspires us—a painting\, a building
 \, a fashion collection\, a photograph\, a piece of music\, a place\, or e
 ven an everyday object that changes the way we see the world.  In collabor
 ation with the Art Therapy Program at the Eskenazi Museum\, Art That Chang
 ed Me invites attendees to share one image (physical or digital) and one s
 tory about something that has inspired\, challenged\, or shaped who they a
 re.  Through brief 3–5 minute presentations\, participants will celebrat
 e the diverse experiences\, passions\, and creative journeys that make up 
 our community while exploring the powerful connections between creativity
 \, reflection\, and wellbeing.  Participants are encouraged to bring their
  content ready to go on a flash drive to enable ease of loading in for the
 ir presentations quickly.
GEO:39.169144;-86.519739
LAST-MODIFIED:20261023T143428Z
LOCATION:SIDNEY AND LOIS ESKENAZI MUSEUM OF ART
URL:https://events.iu.edu/artmuseum/event/2461720-art-that-changed-me-one-
 image-one-story
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Art can be anything that inspires us—a
  painting\, a building\, a fashion collection\, a photograph\, a piece of 
 music\, a place\, or even an everyday object that changes the way we see t
 he world.</p><p>  In collaboration with the Art Therapy Program at the Esk
 enazi Museum\, <i>Art That Changed Me</i> invites attendees to share one i
 mage (physical or digital) and one story about something that has inspired
 \, challenged\, or shaped who they are.</p><p>  Through brief 3–5 minute
  presentations\, participants will celebrate the diverse experiences\, pas
 sions\, and creative journeys that make up our community while exploring t
 he powerful connections between creativity\, reflection\, and wellbeing.</
 p><p class="elementToProof">  Participants are encouraged to bring their c
 ontent ready to go on a flash drive to enable ease of loading in for their
  presentations quickly.</p>
