 s, seminars, and conferences,Performances, shows, and films,Volunteer and 
 fundraising opportunities
DESCRIPTION:With the cold weather approaching\, the November First Thursda
 ys will bring its celebration of art\, ideas\, and community inside. The e
 vent will take place at several indoor spaces across campus\, including IU
  Auditorium (https://www.iuauditorium.com/)\, Eskenazi Museum of Art (http
 s://artmuseum.indiana.edu/)\, Grunwald Gallery (https://eskenazi.indiana.e
 du/exhibitions/grunwald-gallery/index.html)\, Lilly Library (https://libra
 ries.indiana.edu/lilly-library)\, Wells Library (https://libraries.indiana
 .edu/herman-b-wells-library)\, Wylie House Museum (https://libraries.india
 na.edu/wylie-house-museum)\, McCalla (https://collections.iu.edu/mccalla/v
 isit.html)\, and Ford-Crawford Hall (https://music.indiana.edu/news-events
 /directions-parking/index.html). Each space will host its own lineup of ac
 tivities and offer special giveaways. IU Students can also use a special c
 ampus shuttle to get around to all participating venues! For the full list
  of locations\, activities\, and giveaway details\, please visit go.iu.edu
 /first-thursdays (https://artsandhumanities.indiana.edu/council-programs/f
 irst-thursdays/index.html).
