 skenazi Museum of Art\, including the <i>Samuel Levi Jones: An Archeology 
 of Knowledge</i> exhibition\, we'll consider sustainability beyond the env
 ironment and explore what we value—and hope for —in building a future 
 for generations to come.<br /><br /><strong>About Your Guide</strong></p><
 p data-olk-copy-source="MessageBody">  Blake Nietert is a Marketing\, Inte
 rnational\, and Sustainable Business major with a minor in Art History. Wi
 th five semesters of experience leading tours at the Eskenazi Museum of Ar
 t\, he is slowly convincing himself that he has seen the artworks move whe
 n no one is watching.</p><p>  While especially passionate about European a
 rt\, Blake loves exploring and researching art from around the world. He f
 inds that the Eskenazi Museum of Art always offers a new perspective on li
 fe when he needs it most. Blake leads Art Investigator Tours\, Teen Galler
 y Walks\, and a variety of specialty tours\, sharing his enthusiasm for ar
 t and creating engaging experiences for museum visitors</p><p>  &#160\;</p
 ><h3>  Know Before You Go</h3><ul><li data-leveltext="" data-font="Symb
