DESCRIPTION:Highlighting a variety of works in the Eskenazi Museum of Art
 \, including the Samuel Levi Jones: An Archeology of Knowledge exhibition
 \, we'll consider sustainability beyond the environment and explore what w
 e value—and hope for —in building a future for generations to come.Abo
 ut Your Guide  Blake Nietert is a Marketing\, International\, and Sustaina
 ble Business major with a minor in Art History. With five semesters of exp
 erience leading tours at the Eskenazi Museum of Art\, he is slowly convinc
 ing himself that he has seen the artworks move when no one is watching.  W
 hile especially passionate about European art\, Blake loves exploring and 
 researching art from around the world. He finds that the Eskenazi Museum o
 f Art always offers a new perspective on life when he needs it most. Blake
  leads Art Investigator Tours\, Teen Gallery Walks\, and a variety of spec
 ialty tours\, sharing his enthusiasm for art and creating engaging experie
 nces for museum visitors  &#160\;  Know Before You GoWalk-ins are welcome 
 if space is available. Check in with Guest Services on the first floor.&#1
 60\;A small handbag may be carried at your side. Backpacks and large bags 
 will need to be stored before touring. Learn more aboutmuseum guidelines.I
 f you park in the IMU parking lot\, Guest Services can validate your parki
 ng voucher for a discount.Read aboutwhere to find us and where to park\,
