BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Comedy Attic": "https://www.comedyattic.com/shows/378238"}
X-SOURCE-ID:comedy_attic
SUMMARY:Eric Andre: Subtle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261106T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261106T210000
UID:20261106-eric-andre-subtle-1900
DESCRIPTION:ERIC ANDRE is a comedian\, actor and creator and host of Adult
  Swim’s hit series “The Eric Andre Show\,” for which he won an Emmy 
 Award.  He stars in the upcoming Netflix feature LITTLE BROTHER\, directed
  by Matt Spicer\, and recently appeared in HAPPY GILMORE 2 and Peter Farre
 lly’s BALLS UP.  In 2023\, he was featured as an expert panelist on ABC
 ’s “The Prank Panel\,” alongside Johnny Knoxville and Gabourey Sidib
 e\, and launched his first podcast “Bombing with Eric Andre” as part o
 f the iHeartMedia and Will Ferrell’s Big Money Players Network. On the p
 odcast\, Andre asks his guest\, usually a comedian or other type of perfor
 mer\, what their worst experience in front of an audience was\, the worst 
 bombing they’ve ever seen\, and the most wasted they’ve ever been on s
 tage. In 2022\, Andre delivered a hilarious performance not to be missed i
 n season two of HBO’s “The Righteous Gemstones” as ‘Lyle Lissons\,
 ’ a megachurch pastor from Texas who befriends Danny McBride’s ‘Jess
 e Gemstone.’   That same year\, he also starred in an episode of the Net
 flix anthology series “Guillermo del Toro’s Cabinet of Curiosities.”
  In 2020\, his first standup special “Legalize Everything” received cr
 itical praise when it premiered on Netflix and in 2021\, he starred in the
  Netflix comedy BAD TRIP\, which he produced and co-wrote with his directo
 r (Kitao Sakurai) from “The Eric Andre Show.” Co-starring Lil Rel Howe
 ry and Tiffany Haddish\, the film was the #1 most viewed feature world-wid
 e on the platform the first week of its release and marks a major moment i
 n Andre’s career as it takes what he’s been doing with his comedy to t
 he next level.   According to Howard Stern\, “I believe this is gonna wi
 n an Academy Award.”  He added\, “I was laughing so hard I thought my 
 ribs might break.” Andre recently voiced ‘John Dory\,’ the brother o
 f Justin Timberlake’s ‘Branch’ in TROLLS BAND TOGETHER\, as well as 
 the demon ‘Luci’ on the Netflix animated series “Disenchantment” f
 rom creator Matt Groening.  He also lent his voice to the animated action 
 comedy THE MITCHELLS VS. THE MACHINES\, the animated feature SING 2\, and 
 the hyena ‘Azizi’ in Disney’s reimagining of THE LION KING\, from di
 rector Jon Favreau. With an already proven standup act\, Andre decided to 
 break into the world of late-night talk shows. But\, of course\, he brings
  his own flare to what is otherwise a very organized and predictable late-
 night routine. Unlike his counterparts\, Jimmy Fallon or Conan O’Brien\,
  Andre’s unrelenting and constantly over the top humor puts some of his 
 guests on “The Eric Andre Show” into situations they never thought the
 y would end up in. “The Eric Andre Show” is a live-action-comedy telev
 ision series that premiered in May 2012 on Cartoon Network’s Adult Swim.
  Andre was also seen on the big screen in ROUGH NIGHT\, with Scarlett Joha
 nsson and Kate McKinnon.  His other film credits include POPSTAR: NEVER ST
 OP NEVER STOPPING\, with Andy Samberg\, and THE INTERNSHIP\, with Vince Va
 ughn and Owen Wilson. Andre starred on FXX’s “Man Seeking Woman” for
  three seasons from 2015 to 2017\, with Jay Baruchel.  He was also a serie
 s regular on ABC’s “Don’t Trust the B---- in Apt. 23.”
LOCATION:The Comedy Attic\, 123 S Walnut Street\, Bloomington\, IN
URL:https://www.comedyattic.com/shows/378238
X-SOURCE:The Comedy Attic
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events Livewhale 130": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2361635-guided-tours-of-the-lilly-library"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_130
SUMMARY:Guided tours of the Lilly Library
DTSTART:20261106T190000Z
DTEND:20261106T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20260727T114729Z
UID:20261106T190000Z-2361726@events.iu.edu__20261106
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/261/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,768,512/10121_Lilly_Library.exteror.web_.rev.1639508831.j
 pg
CATEGORIES:Art and museum exhibitions
DESCRIPTION:You'll visit the Lilly's main galleries\, and your expert guid
 e will talk about some of the Lilly's highlights including the Gutenberg B
 ible&#160\;and our current exhibitions from the Lilly Library collections:
  The Declaration of Independence: The Motives\, the Moment (https://librar
 ies.indiana.edu/lilly-library/declaration-independence) and The Signers (h
 ttps://libraries.indiana.edu/lilly-library/the-signers). Additional hands-
 on time with rotating selections from the collections will follow. These s
 elections include medieval manuscripts\, artists books\, and one of the Jo
 hn Ford's Best Director Oscars. Non-flash photography is permitted\, seati
 ng is available throughout the tour\, and the building is wheelchair acces
 sible. The tour generally lasts a little less than one hour and is open to
  all.
GEO:39.167909;-86.518974
LAST-MODIFIED:20260727T154729Z
LOCATION:Lilly Library (1200 E. Seventh St.)
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2361635-guided-tours-of-the-lilly-li
 brary
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  You'll visit the Lilly's main galleries
 \, and your expert guide will talk about some of the Lilly's highlights in
 cluding the Gutenberg Bible&#160\;and our current exhibitions from the Lil
 ly Library collections: <em><a href="https://libraries.indiana.edu/lilly-l
 ibrary/declaration-independence" target="_blank" rel="noopener">The Declar
 ation of Independence: The Motives\, the Moment</a></em> and <em><a href="
 https://libraries.indiana.edu/lilly-library/the-signers" target="_blank" r
 el="noopener">The Signers</a></em>. Additional hands-on time with rotating
  selections from the collections will follow. These selections include med
 ieval manuscripts\, artists books\, and one of the John Ford's Best Direct
 or Oscars. Non-flash photography is permitted\, seating is available throu
 ghout the tour\, and the building is wheelchair accessible. The tour gener
 ally lasts a little less than one hour and is open to all.</p>
