BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Visit Bloomington": "https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/aanikoobijigan-w-qa-additional-films-and-guests/59995/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:visit_bloomington
SUMMARY:Aanikoobijigan w/ Q&A | Additional Films and Guests
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261107T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261107T150000
UID:a273e8bff326e03bde1cdf8ee0d4b39f@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:"What's the difference between an archaeologist and a grave ro
 bber?" an elder asks. "A degree\," he laughs. Aanikoobijigan examines the 
 ongoing struggle to repatriate Indigenous ancestors' remains from museums 
 and archives\, exposing the thin line between archaeology and grave robber
 y. With striking visuals and grounded Indigenous perspectives\, Aanikoobij
 igan challenges institutional resistance to decolonization and affirms tha
 t returning ancestors to the earth restores memory\, dignity\, and balance
 \, reminding us that no community can be whole until their ancestors are f
 inally laid to rest. [80 min\; documentary\; English and Anishinaabemowin 
 with English subtitles]\nThe screening will be followed by a conversation 
 between IU Indianapolis professor Dr. Holly Cusack-McVeigh (Anthropology a
 nd Museum Studies\; Public Scholar of Collections and Community Curation)
 —who is featured in the film—and Dr. Jayne-Leigh Thomas (Executive Dir
 ector\, Office of the Native American Graves Protection and Repatriation A
 ct\, Indiana University).
GEO:39.168585;-86.517361
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 E. 7th Street\, Bloomington\, IN 47405
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/aanikoobijigan-w-qa-additional-
 films-and-guests/59995/
X-SOURCE:Visit Bloomington
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/events/
END:VEVENT
