X-SOURCE-ID:gcal_c_25e52423b2d0772255c59d0e398b655d5c121833814b7b9fc11f4ddd9cff195c_group_calendar_google_com
SUMMARY:Redbud Books Fall Reading Group: Solidarity With Children by Madel
 ine Lane-McKinley
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261108T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261108T123000
DTSTAMP:20261031T043533Z
UID:4r8aclagl68mtijodsttt7p5fj@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20261108T110000
SEQUENCE:0
CREATED:20260917T190513Z
DESCRIPTION:Solidarity with Children makes a provocative case for child li
 beration and asks us to rethink what it means to be in relationship with c
 hildren—to care for them\, work with them\, raise them\, and imagine a d
 ifferent kind of solidarity with them.\n\nThis conversation is for parents
 \, educators\, caregivers\, youth workers\, and anyone who wants to interr
 ogate their own relationship to children and the structures that shape it.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260917T190513Z
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-SOURCE:Redbud Books
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Brown County State Park": "https://events.in.gov/event/copy-of-autumn-leaves-revisited-brown-county-state-park-2613"}
X-SOURCE-ID:localist_brown_county_sp
SUMMARY:Autumn Leaves Revisited\, Brown County State Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261108T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261108T113000
UID:4624f9993373a2a66e316cc7ab453dd5@events.in.gov
DESCRIPTION:Have you ever wondered how and why our forests change into the
 ir beautiful fall colors? This program explains just that! Join a naturali
 st as we walk through how leaves transform through the seasons and why the
 y turn into the colors we see in the fall on the microscopic level! Stick 
 around after the program for a fun coloring activity to help you recognize
  and remember what changes our green leaves into yellows\, oranges\, reds
 \, and browns.
LOCATION:Brown County State Park\, Nature Center program room\, 1405 S.R. 
 46 W\, Nashville\, IN 
URL:https://events.in.gov/event/copy-of-autumn-leaves-revisited-brown-coun
 ty-state-park-2613
X-SOURCE:Brown County State Park
END:VEVENT
