X-SOURCE-ID:gcal_48ac7e6a73bd950b28dea0eca41b3050858f0c4f00ddfbd78dd23a2a9e5fc51d
SUMMARY:Daughters of the King - Meeting
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261109T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261109T190000
DTSTAMP:20261031T043537Z
UID:6ldoglgmrft5fg85ovj42pq6a2_R20260309T213000@google.com__20261109
SEQUENCE:0
CREATED:20250310T211808Z
DESCRIPTION:<p><br>Daughters of the King “DOK” is a world-wide religio
 us order founded in 1885 by Episcopal women. Today it includes women from 
 a wide variety of Christian traditions. Members of the DOK are ordinary wo
 men who are married and single\, live in the world\, and dedicate themselv
 es prayer\, service and evangelism. Monthly gatherings include educational
  programs\; recent programs at Trinity have highlighted Amish communities 
 of faith\, virtual prayer retreats\, handling conflict\, book reviews\, th
 e Lenten season\, Mary Magdalene\, and many other topics related to Christ
 ian faith and life. Members help with church events throughout the year.</
 p><p>Trinity’s chapter usually meets on the <strong>2nd Monday of the m
 onth at 5:00 pm</strong> in the Church Library\; check the announcements 
 in the Sunday worship bulletin for any change in location. All women inter
 ested in loving service and spiritual fellowship are welcome. For more inf
 ormation contact the Rev. Virginia Hall at <a href="mailto:yesvirginia194
 2@gmail.com">yesvirginia1942@gmail.com</a> or Heather Lake at <a href="m
 ailto:hr42lake@gmail.com">hr42lake@gmail.com</a>.</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260221T162554Z
LOCATION:Library
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-SOURCE:Trinity Episcopal Church
END:VEVENT
