BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Visit Bloomington": "https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/vindication-swim-w-qa-additional-films-and-guests/59997/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:visit_bloomington
SUMMARY:Vindication Swim w/ Q&A | Additional Films and Guests
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261109T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261109T211500
UID:20810c13b46835dbe410f272d9f6008b@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:Vindication Swim tells the remarkable story of Mercedes Gleitz
 e\, who in 1927 became the first British woman to swim the English Channel
 . Facing press hostility\, anti-immigrant bias\, and constraints on women 
 in sport\, Mercedes’ achievement remains a powerful testament to her gri
 t\, courage\, and determination. Writer-director Elliott Hasler—only 23 
 when the film premiered—pursued period authenticity through grassroots c
 ollaboration with coastal communities throughout the UK. Three years in th
 e making\, the film’s swimming sequences were shot miles out in the Chan
 nel\, vividly capturing the perils of Mercedes’ epic crossing. [98 min\;
  drama\; English]\nA Q&A with director Elliott Hasler and Radhika Paramesw
 aran (Herman B Wells Endowed Professor\, Media School) will follow the scr
 eening.
GEO:39.168585;-86.517361
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 E. 7th Street\, Bloomington\, IN 47405
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/vindication-swim-w-qa-additiona
 l-films-and-guests/59997/
X-SOURCE:Visit Bloomington
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/events/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"WFIU Community Calendar": "https://www.ipm.org/community-calendar/event/vindication-swim-screening-and-filmmaker-q-amp-a-26-10-2026-11-20-03"}
X-SOURCE-ID:wfiu_community_calendar
SUMMARY:Vindication Swim- Screening and Filmmaker Q&A
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261109T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261109T213000
UID:3ba630eb82531feee39187a4f6a3283e@ipm.org
DESCRIPTION:Presented by IU School of Public Health- Bloomington and The M
 edia School\nVindication Swim (2024)\, will screen at the IU Cinema\, foll
 owed by a live audience Q&A with British independent filmmaker Elliott Has
 ler.\n Vindication Swim tells the remarkable true story of Mercedes Gleitz
 e\, a working-class typist and daughter of German immigrants who\, in 1927
 \, became the first British woman to swim the English Channel. In an era w
 hen women faced significant social barriers and female athletes struggled 
 for recognition\, Gleitze achieved an extraordinary feat of endurance. The
  film celebrates a pioneering athlete whose determination carried her thro
 ugh physical hardship\, prejudice\, and a fight for the recognition she de
 served.\n The film itself has a remarkable story behind it. Its swimming s
 equences were filmed miles offshore in the actual English Channel\, with l
 ead actress Kirsten Callaghan performing her own swimming—without tanks
 \, green screens\, or body doubles.\n The event is co-sponsored by the IU 
 School of Public Health–Bloomington and The Media School.\nTickets: &#xa
 0\;go.iu.edu/vindicationswim
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 East 7th Street\, Bloomington\, Indiana 47405
URL:https://www.ipm.org/community-calendar/event/vindication-swim-screenin
 g-and-filmmaker-q-amp-a-26-10-2026-11-20-03
X-SOURCE:WFIU Community Calendar
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.ipm.org/community-calendar/
END:VEVENT
