DESCRIPTION:Rhonda and Anthony Moravec Gallery\, Center for Prints\, Drawi
 ngs\, and Photographs\, Third Floor  This hour-long gallery conversation b
 rings together perspectives from contemporary artandthelaw. Guestsreflecto
 nJones'spowerfulworkandexplorequestionsofhistory\,systemsofknowledge\,powe
 r\,andrepresentation.  Featured guests:I. India Thusi&#160\;is a Professor
  of Law and Charles L. Whistler Faculty Fellow at the Indiana University M
 aurer School of Law and a Senior Scientist at the Kinsey Institute. Her sc
 holarship examines how law constructs\, regulates\, and polices race\, sex
 uality\, vice\, and gender. She is the author of Policing Bodies: Law\, Se
 x Work\, and Desire in Johannesburg (Stanford University Press)\, an ethno
 graphic and legal study of sex work policing in South Africa. Her articles
  have appeared in the Harvard Law Review\, New York University Law Review
 \, California Law Review\, Northwestern University Law Review\, Georgetown
  Law Journal\, UCLA Law Review\, and other leading journals.&#160\;Elliot 
 Josephine Leila Reichert is an American curator\, critic\, and editor. She
  is the inaugural Curator of Contemporary Art at the Eskenazi Museum of Ar
 t at Indiana University and was a 2023-24 Propel Fellow with the Associati
 on of Art Museum Curators Foundation. Reichert has curated critically accl
 aimed exhibitions and published widely in leading art journals.
