  Center for Prints\, Drawings\, and Photographs\, Third Floor</p><p class=
 "font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">  
 This hour-long gallery conversation brings together perspectives from cont
 emporary <span class="___1cs5bdp f1w7gpdv f5p0z4x">art</span><span class="
 ___1cs5bdp f1w7gpdv f5p0z4x">and</span><span class="___1cs5bdp f1w7gpdv f5
 p0z4x">the</span><span class="___1cs5bdp f1w7gpdv f5p0z4x">law.</span> G<s
 pan class="___1cs5bdp f1w7gpdv f5p0z4x">uests</span><span class="___1cs5bd
 p f1w7gpdv f5p0z4x">reflect</span><span class="___1cs5bdp f1w7gpdv f5p0z4x
 ">on</span><span class="___1cs5bdp f1w7gpdv f5p0z4x">Jones's</span><span c
 lass="___1cs5bdp f1w7gpdv f5p0z4x">powerful</span><span class="___1cs5bdp 
 f1w7gpdv f5p0z4x">work</span><span class="___1cs5bdp f1w7gpdv f5p0z4x">and
 </span><span class="___1cs5bdp f1w7gpdv f5p0z4x">explore</span><span class
 ="___1cs5bdp f1w7gpdv f5p0z4x">questions</span><span class="___1cs5bdp f1w
 7gpdv f5p0z4x">of</span><span class="___1cs5bdp f1w7gpdv f5p0z4x">history
 \,</span><span class="___1cs5bdp f1w7gpdv f5p0z4x">systems</span><span cla
 ss="___1cs5bdp f1w7gpdv f5p0z4x">of</span><span class="___1cs5bdp f1w7gpdv
  f5p0z4x">knowledge\,</span><span class="___1cs5bdp f1w7gpdv f5p0z4x">powe
 r\,</span><span class="___1cs5bdp f1w7gpdv f5p0z4x">and</span><span class=
 "___1cs5bdp f1w7gpdv f5p0z4x">representation.</span></p><p class="font-cla
 ude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">  Featured 
 guests:</p><p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-norm
 al leading-[1.7]"><strong>I. India Thusi</strong>&#160\;is a Professor of 
 Law and Charles L. Whistler Faculty Fellow at the Indiana University Maure
 r School of Law and a Senior Scientist at the Kinsey Institute. Her schola
 rship examines how law constructs\, regulates\, and polices race\, sexuali
 ty\, vice\, and gender. She is the author of Policing Bodies: Law\, Sex Wo
 rk\, and Desire in Johannesburg (Stanford University Press)\, an ethnograp
 hic and legal study of sex work policing in South Africa. Her articles hav
 e appeared in the Harvard Law Review\, New York University Law Review\, Ca
 lifornia Law Review\, Northwestern University Law Review\, Georgetown Law 
 Journal\, UCLA Law Review\, and other leading journals.&#160\;</p><p class
 ="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]"><
 strong>Elliot Josephine Leila Reichert</strong> is an American curator\, c
 ritic\, and editor. She is the inaugural Curator of Contemporary Art at th
 e Eskenazi Museum of Art at Indiana University and was a 2023-24 Propel Fe
 llow with the Association of Art Museum Curators Foundation. Reichert has 
 curated critically acclaimed exhibitions and published widely in leading a
 rt journals.</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-CONTACT-INFO:<p>\n  Emily Zarse<br />\n  Public Experiences Ma
 nager<br />\n  eczarse@iu.edu\n</p>
