 #160\;        </p><p style="text-align: center\;"><strong><em>By Their Own
  Hands: The Black Filmmakers Hall of Fame!</em></strong></p><p>          F
 ounded in 1974 by the Culture and Ethnic Affairs Guild of the Oakland Muse
 um of California\, the Black Filmmakers Hall of Fame began as a film lectu
 re series and awards ceremony celebrating achievements of Black film indus
 try figures. When that organization closed\, they donated their materials 
 to IU. In collaboration with the IU Black Film Center and Archive\, this e
 xhibit features objects from that collection\, including founding document
 s\, costumes\, and handprints of inductees to the Hall of Fame.        </p
