DESCRIPTION:Come join moderator Nikos Zirogiannis (https://oneill.indiana.
 edu/faculty-research/directory/profiles/faculty/full-time/zirogiannis-niko
 laos.html) (O'Neill School) and five other IUB faculty members as they sha
 re the one thing you need to know about climate change.Christopher Callaha
 n (https://oneill.indiana.edu/faculty-research/directory/profiles/faculty/
 full-time/callahan-christopher.html) (O'Neill)\, Rebecca Dirksen (https://
 folklore.indiana.edu/about/faculty/dirksen-rebecca.html) (Folklore &amp\; 
 Ethnomusicology)\, Sara Gregg (https://history.indiana.edu/faculty_staff/f
 aculty/gregg_sara.html) (History)\, Kim Novick (https://oneill.indiana.edu
 /faculty-research/directory/profiles/faculty/full-time/novick-kimberly.htm
 l) (O'Neill and ESSI (https://environment.indiana.edu/index.html))\, and S
 pencer Perry (https://education.indiana.edu/news/2026/jul-dec/2026-08-20-i
 usoe-welcomes-new-faculty.html) (School of Education) will each share five
  minutes of what they want us to know about climate change.  These talks w
 ill be followed by discussion and Q&amp\;A. This event is sponsored by IU'
 s Institute for Advanced Study (https://ias.indiana.edu/). All IU and Bloo
 mington community members are invited to attend and learn with us during t
 his IU Climate Week (https://eri.iu.edu/news-and-events/events/iu-climate-
 week.html) event.
