SUMMARY:CMLT-C 291: STUDIES IN NON-WESTERN FILM (Izabela Potapowicz)
DESCRIPTION:Emphasis on non-Western film in relation to literary and 
 cultural texts. Films may be studied as adaptations of literary works\, as 
 reworkings of generic or ideological traditions\, and in their engagement 
 with the aesthetics of non-Western theater and Hollywood. Focus on one 
 regional tradition (African\, Asian\, Middle Eastern) each time the course 
 is offered.
LOCATION:Wells Screening Room (ground floor\, within Media Services)
ORGANIZER;CN="Jamie Thomas":MAILTO:jt85@iu.edu
