SUMMARY:McCalla Center Open Gallery Hours
DTSTART:20261112T160000Z
DTEND:20261112T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20260716T121602Z
UID:20261103T160000Z-2387762@events.iu.edu__20261112
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/479/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,3200,2400/27084_McCalla_Southeast_Side.rev.1753275924.jpg
CATEGORIES:Art, music, films, and performances,Art and museum exhibitions,
 Community events,Functions, festivals, and celebrations
DESCRIPTION:Outfitting IU Athletics: Hoosier Champions                  Th
 is exhibit showcases objects from IU's championship teams and athletes\, c
 onnecting them to historic achievements in the Big Ten and the national st
 age. The items featured in the exhibit are from the IU Athletics Sports Me
 morabilia Collection and feature photos and videos provided by IU Athletic
 s and Indiana University Archives.                Dates: November 14\, 202
 5 - October 2026          &#160\;                  &#160\;        By Their
  Own Hands: The Black Filmmakers Hall of Fame!          Founded in 1974 by
  the Culture and Ethnic Affairs Guild of the Oakland Museum of California
 \, the Black Filmmakers Hall of Fame began as a film lecture series and aw
 ards ceremony celebrating achievements of Black film industry figures. Whe
 n that organization closed\, they donated their materials to IU. In collab
 oration with the IU Black Film Center and Archive\, this exhibit features 
 objects from that collection\, including founding documents\, costumes\, a
 nd handprints of inductees to the Hall of Fame.        Dates: September 20
 25 - December 2026          &#160\;                  &#160\;        Captur
 ing the Campus: T.C. Steele\, Indiana University's First Artist in Residen
 ceCapturing the Campus pays tribute to renowned Hoosier artist T.C. Steele
 . The exhibit honors the century that has passed since his death by showca
 sing paintings form the artist's residency at IU and other relevant works.
  The exhibit will bring together Steele's landscapes from the IU Public Ar
 t and Cultural Heritage Collection and the Indiana State Museum and Histor
 ic Sites' collection\, allowing the holdings of these two collections to b
 e viewed in one space.        Dates: April 17\, 2026 - April 2026         
  &#160\;        Multipurpose Room          Currently Featuring: The Gift o
 f Collecting: Tina Jernigan          Jernigan was a passionate supporter o
 f both Indiana University and the arts. She donated artworks to the IU Pub
 lic Art and Cultural Heritage Collection upon her passing in 2024. With fu
 nding provided by Jernigan\, Public Art professionally framed\, hung\, and
  preserved these pieces for this exhibit in the McCalla Building and for f
 uture installations on campus.&#160\;        Dates: July 2026-July 2027&#1
 60\;  &#160\;  &#160\;  &#160\;
LAST-MODIFIED:20260904T142940Z
