X-SOURCE-ID:visit_bloomington
SUMMARY:Margaret Bourke-White & Sunil Janah: A Photographic Collaboration 
 opening reception
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261112T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261112T180000
UID:dce2488fe3ead8428fb178d9cf13ca3b@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:Curated by CAHI Director Alex Lichtenstein\, the exhibition br
 ings together 29 works by two giants of twentieth century documentary phot
 ography. Together\, their work documents the drama of Partition\, the trag
 edy of famine\, the dignity of labor\, and the story of India’s march to
  Independence and modernity.
GEO:39.1709246;-86.527549
LOCATION:McCalla Center\, 525 E. 9th St.\, Bloomington\, IN 47408
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/margaret-bourke-white-sunil-jan
 ah-a-photographic-collaboration-opening-reception/60160/
