BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"WFIU Community Calendar": "https://www.ipm.org/community-calendar/event/margaret-bourke-white-amp-sunil-janah-a-photographic-collaboration-29-10-2026-13-03-22"}
X-SOURCE-ID:wfiu_community_calendar
SUMMARY:Margaret Bourke-White & Sunil Janah: A Photographic Collaboration
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261112T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261112T180000
UID:644b5e8f5b3ff24c11f6671362b18f4e@ipm.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims4/default/e53a
 8b5/2147483647/strip/true/crop/879x498+0+0/resize/254x144!/quality/90/?url
 =http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F9c%2Fda%2F7047b2fa4fa29161
 4ac7bc2dae44%2F11r.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Presented by McCalla Center\n"Margaret Bourke-White & Sunil Ja
 nah: A Photographic Collaboration" brings into conversation two of the mos
 t important photographers of modern India\, Sunil Janah (1918–2012) and 
 Margaret Bourke-White (1904–1971)\, whose lives and photographic practic
 es intersected during India’s transition to independence. Drawing on pho
 tographs from across their careers\, the works document the drama of Parti
 tion\, the tragedy of famine\, the dignity of labor\, and the story of Ind
 ia’s march to Independence and modernity.\n Accompanied by historical te
 xts and related print ephemera\, the exhibition demonstrates the deeply co
 llaborative and transnational character of mid-twentieth-century documenta
 ry photography. \n Margaret Bourke-White & Sunil Janah: A Photographic Col
 laboration is curated by Dr. Alex Lichtenstein\, Ruth N. Halls Professor o
 f History and American Studies and Director of the College of Arts and Hum
 anities Institute at Indiana University. The exhibition is sponsored by Dh
 ar India Studies Program\, Department of History\, the Center for Document
 ary Research and Practice\, IUB Arts & Humanities Council\, the McCalla Ce
 nter\, and IU’s Office of the Vice President of International Affairs.\n
  The exhibition is free and open to the public.
LOCATION:McCalla Center\, 525 East 9th Street\, Bloomington\, Indiana 4740
 8
URL:https://www.ipm.org/community-calendar/event/margaret-bourke-white-amp
 -sunil-janah-a-photographic-collaboration-29-10-2026-13-03-22
X-SOURCE:WFIU Community Calendar
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.ipm.org/community-calendar/
END:VEVENT
