DESCRIPTION:Students will look closely at still life paintings in the gall
 eries\, discovering how artists use symbolism and lighting to communicate 
 mood and reveal more than meets the eye. After finding inspiration in the 
 galleries\, students will create their own still life paintings by arrangi
 ng and observing objects at their table to tell their own unique stories! 
  Program designed by our licensed art educator for students in grades K-12
 .Know Before You Go:  Meet us in the Simpson Center for Education on the 2
 nd floor of the museum at 1 pm. Together\, we'll drop off personal items b
 efore exploring the galleries. After seeing artworks that will inspire our
  project\, we'll head back to the Roehm Family Art-Making Studio to create
  our own masterpieces! Don't forget to dress for a mess!  Strollers are we
 lcome. Chaperone required. We ask that chaperones be 18 or older\, with on
 e adult for every 6 children.
