BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-ID:gcal_d1087e97d4ace1c1ca2dd6336d417bea870ddac277be6d1711cbc0235aa85228
SUMMARY:Discardia Mending Day
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261114T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261114T160000
DTSTAMP:20261031T043417Z
UID:1nkkv7oc4quoqmepjuh7pu2ivt@google.com__20261114
SEQUENCE:0
CREATED:20230708T144833Z
DESCRIPTION:<h2>Mending Day is the second Saturday of each month\, noon ti
 ll 4PM. Join our sewing circle as we teach\, learn\, help others\, mend an
 d create art.<br>Please be kind and pre-launder your projects.<br></h2><br
 >Bring your sewing\, interest in sewing\, interest to learn\, and willingn
 ess to teach\, or just bring pre-washed fabric items in need of mending or
  alteration! We fix and alter garments and other fabric items for free\, a
 s a service to the greater community\, for fun! Let’s keep things useful
  and out of landfill together!<h2><a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=ht
 tps://www.bloomingtonvolunteernetwork.org/need/detail/?need_id%3D355829&am
 p\;sa=D&amp\;source=calendar&amp\;usd=2&amp\;usg=AOvVaw3EzRHKM1FFCzDTiJ_96
 3K2" target="_blank">Calling all Artists\, Fashion Designers\, Creatives\,
  and Community Members of All Ages Interested in Sustainable Practices. <
 /a></h2><p></p><p>Discardia\, a program of the Center for Sustainable Livi
 ng\, creates an environment for local designers to brainstorm to make upcy
 cled clothing and to teach people in the community how to upcycle their ow
 n items. </p><h3>Get involved with Discardia as a Mending Day Sewing Advi
 sor: <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.bloomingtonvolunte
 ernetwork.org/need/detail/?need_id%3D355829&amp\;sa=D&amp\;source=calendar
 &amp\;usd=2&amp\;usg=AOvVaw3EzRHKM1FFCzDTiJ_963K2" target="_blank">https:/
 /www.bloomingtonvolunteernetwork.org/need/detail/?need_id=355829</a></h3><
 p>Discardia members and volunteer Sewing Advisors assist attendees in mend
 ing clothing\, giving them an opportunity to learn how to sew or work on 
 any other project involving clothing. Sewing machines and basic supplies a
 re provided to participants\, for free\, and all ages are welcome!</p><p>V
 olunteer Sewing Advisors offer help to participants with altering or repai
 ring the garments that they have brought in. Use your skills to assist par
 ticipants with creative solutions\, but not to make all the decisions for 
 them.</p><p>Help is also appreciated in setting up and tearing down before
  and after the event (30 minutes each). </p><p>This is a great way to emp
 ower as well as collaborate with a group of creative problem solvers and l
 earn to use the various tools and tricks of the trade to make it easier to
  make adjustments to our own clothes so that they fit well and are comfort
 able and we feel good wearing them.</p><p>All skill levels are welcome and
  training is provided. It&#39\;s a lot of fun and makes you feel empowered
  and confident. <span>Contact Stephen Hale\, Discardia Project Manager if
  interested at 812-334-0922.</span></p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20230708T144833Z
LOCATION:Monroe County Public Library - Downtown\, 303 E Kirkwood Ave\, Bl
 oomington\, IN 47408\, USA
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-SOURCE:BloomingtonOnline Events
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
