BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Limestone Post": "https://seeconstellation.org/kids/goosebumps/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:limestone_post
SUMMARY:R.L. STINE’S GOOSEBUMPS THE MUSICAL: PHANTOM OF THE AUDITORIUM
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261115T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261115T130000
UID:260917DnMKS5nBZ02Z8fKnfPjH8g
DESCRIPTION:***Spooky fun for the whole family!***\n\n**Get ready for a fr
 ightfully fun adventure with *Goosebumps The Musical\,* based on the wil
 dly popular books by R. L. Stine! When Brooke and Zeke are cast in their s
 chool’s spooky new play\, *The Phantom*\, they start to wonder if the s
 how is actually cursed. As strange messages appear and rehearsals are disr
 upted by a mysterious masked figure\, they must uncover the truth: is it a
 ll an elaborate prank… or is their theater truly haunted? Full of catchy
  songs\, laugh-out-loud moments\, and just the right amount of Halloween-s
 eason chills\, this musical mystery is perfect for kids\, tweens\, and gro
 wn-ups who remember reading by flashlight. *Fun for all ages!*** \n\n**
 “Musically exciting and theatrically adventurous entertainment that is s
 ure to give you goosebumps!” – *BroadwayWorld*** \n\n**Cast Meet and
  Greet: Stick around after the show to meet the cast and get autographs fr
 om your favorite characters!**\n\nSee Constellation’s website for more i
 nformation\, including a detailed performance schedule. Learn more and fin
 d tickets at https://seeconstellation.org/kids/goosebumps/
LOCATION:Waldron Auditorium
URL:https://seeconstellation.org/kids/goosebumps/
X-SOURCE:Limestone Post
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Visit Bloomington": "https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/the-christophers-art-and-a-movie/60002/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:visit_bloomington
SUMMARY:The Christophers | Art and a Movie
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261115T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261115T151500
UID:8b569902aa849e24666165ef80d57ae2@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:Julian Sklar (Ian McKellen) was once a star of London’s 1960
 s and '70s pop art explosion\, but he hasn’t painted in decades and has 
 been broke for years. His two estranged children (James Corden\, Jessica G
 unning)\, desperate for an inheritance\, hire Lori\, an art restorer and f
 ormer forger (Michaela Coel)\, to pose as a prospective assistant in order
  to access eight unfinished canvases Julian has buried deep in storage. He
 r plan is to complete them\, then return them to storage\, where they are 
 to be “discovered” upon Julian’s death. [100 min\; comedy\, drama\; 
 English]\nThis program is presented in partnership with the Eskenazi Museu
 m of Art. After the screening\, a 30-minute discussion themed around the f
 ilm will take place at the museum. More details to come!
GEO:39.168585;-86.517361
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 E. 7th Street\, Bloomington\, IN 47405
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/the-christophers-art-and-a-movi
 e/60002/
X-SOURCE:Visit Bloomington
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/events/
END:VEVENT
