X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_234
SUMMARY:The Christophers | Art and a Movie
DTSTART:20261115T180000Z
DTEND:20261115T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20261012T164141Z
UID:20261115T180000Z-2448587@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20261115T180000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/81/width/168/height/168/crop/1
 /src_region/0,0,1921,1080/32998_The_Christophers_1920x1080.rev.1791672087.
 png
CATEGORIES:Culture and languages,Performances, shows, and films
DESCRIPTION:Julian Sklar (Ian McKellen) was once a star of London's 1960s 
 and '70s pop art explosion\, but he hasn't painted in decades and has been
  broke for years. His two estranged children (James Corden\, Jessica Gunni
 ng)\, desperate for an inheritance\, hire Lori\, an art restorer and forme
 r forger (Michaela Coel)\, to pose as a prospective assistant in order to 
 access eight unfinished canvases Julian has buried deep in storage. Her pl
 an is to complete them\, then return them to storage\, where they are to b
 e "discovered" upon Julian's death. [100 min\; comedy\, drama\; English]Th
 is program is presented in partnership with the Eskenazi Museum of Art. Af
 ter the screening\, continue the conversation at the Eskenazi Museum of Ar
 t with a special program led by Jean Graves\, Meier Chair of Education\, f
 ocused on how objects in the museum&#8217\;s collections have been affecte
 d by conservators\, restorers\, assistants\, and the original artists them
 selves. Register for this free event here.
GEO:39.168613;-86.517376
LAST-MODIFIED:20261029T190745Z
LOCATION:IU CINEMA
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2446642-the-christophers-art-and-a-m
 ovie
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Julian Sklar (Ian McKellen) was once a s
 tar of London's 1960s and '70s pop art explosion\, but he hasn't painted i
 n decades and has been broke for years. His two estranged children (James 
 Corden\, Jessica Gunning)\, desperate for an inheritance\, hire Lori\, an 
 art restorer and former forger (Michaela Coel)\, to pose as a prospective 
 assistant in order to access eight unfinished canvases Julian has buried d
 eep in storage. Her plan is to complete them\, then return them to storage
 \, where they are to be "discovered" upon Julian's death. [100 min\; comed
 y\, drama\; English]</p><p><i><strong>This program is presented in partner
 ship with the Eskenazi Museum of Art. After the screening\, continue the c
 onversation at the Eskenazi Museum of Art with a special program led by Je
 an Graves\, Meier Chair of Education\, focused on how objects in the museu
 m&#8217\;s collections have been affected by conservators\, restorers\, as
 sistants\, and the original artists themselves. Register for this free eve
 nt </strong></i><a class="external" href="https://events.iu.edu/bloomingto
 n/event/2457787-art-a-movie-at-the-eskenazi-museum-unfinished-busine"><i><
 strong>here</strong></i></a><i><strong>.</strong></i></p>
