X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_64
SUMMARY:The Evolving Landscape of College Athlete Compensation: A Conversa
 tion with Libby Harmon
DTSTART:20261117T170000Z
DTEND:20261117T180000Z
DTSTAMP:20261016T184610Z
UID:20261117T170000Z-2454513@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20261117T170000Z
CATEGORIES:Student-run
DESCRIPTION:Join the Sports &amp\; Entertainment Law Society (SELS) for a 
 lunch time conversation with a locally based sports law attorney\, Libby H
 armon.  Libby Harmon\, Senior Counsel at Nervius Legal\, represents athlet
 es\, leagues\, and brands shaping the future of sports on complex investig
 ations\, eligibility cases\, commercial transactions\, and regulatory stra
 tegy matters. Before joining Nervius Legal\, she previously worked as the 
 Director of Compliance at the University of Michigan and before that she w
 orked as the Associate Director of Enforcement at the NCAA.&#160\;  Come l
 earn about working with college athletes\, NIL\, athletic compliance\, spo
 rts gambling\, Title IX\, the intersection of business and sports law\, an
 d more!  RSVP by 10 AM on November 16th.&#160\;
GEO:39.165074;-86.526424
LAST-MODIFIED:20261028T003856Z
LOCATION:Lowell E. Baier Hall - Lecture Room - 121
URL:https://events.iu.edu/lawiub/event/2454513-the-evolving-landscape-of-s
 ports-law-a
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Join the Sports &amp\; Entertainment Law
  Society (SELS) for a lunch time conversation with a locally based sports 
 law attorney\, Libby Harmon.</p><p>  Libby Harmon\, Senior Counsel at Nerv
 ius Legal\, represents athletes\, leagues\, and brands shaping the future 
 of sports on complex investigations\, eligibility cases\, commercial trans
 actions\, and regulatory strategy matters. Before joining Nervius Legal\, 
 she previously worked as the Director of Compliance at the University of M
 ichigan and before that she worked as the Associate Director of Enforcemen
 t at the NCAA.&#160\;</p><p>  Come learn about working with college athlet
 es\, NIL\, athletic compliance\, sports gambling\, Title IX\, the intersec
 tion of business and sports law\, and more!</p><p>  RSVP by 10 AM on Novem
 ber 16th.&#160\;</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-CONTACT-INFO:<p>Emily Abramczyk<br />\nSports &amp\; Entertain
 ment Law Society (SELS)</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-ID:2454513
X-LIVEWHALE-RSVP:1
