BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Browncounty": "https://browncounty.com/events/the-allman-betts-family-revival/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:browncounty
SUMMARY:The Allman Betts Family Revival
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261125T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261125T190000
DTSTAMP:20261029T130510Z
UID:MEC-8685017f26d34de83878fcbbc386f3c2@browncounty.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261125T190000
SEQUENCE:3
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://browncounty.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/
 10/2-300x240-4.jpeg
CATEGORIES:Entertainment,Live Music
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20261029
DESCRIPTION:What started as a 70th birthday celebration for Gregg Allman i
 n 2017 has evolved into an annual celebration of one of rock ‘n’ roll
 ’s finest catalogs.  Galvanizing the families of Allman & Betts: The Al
 lman Betts Family Revival has become a yearly tradition featuring some of 
 the finest musicians on the planet\, and will make a stop at the Brown Cou
 nty Music Center in Nashville\, Ind.\, on Sunday\, November 29\, 2026.\nDe
 von and Duane honor their families’ legacies\, evoking the haunting spir
 it of the greats that came before them by gathering a world class ensemble
  cast a la “The Last Waltz\,” with the songs bursting with new fervor 
 nationwide. The Revival stage has seen the likes of Slash\, Jason Isbell\,
  Steve Earle\, Sierra Ferrell\, Marcus King sitting in – while legends l
 ike Jimmy Hall\, Robert Randolph and Amanda Shires have hopped on the bus 
 for the entire coast to coast 2026 jaunt. This year celebrates a DECADE of
  The Allman Betts Family Revival. Leaning on the “decade” theme\, the 
 first set of the show will honor the original lineup and focus on songs fr
 om the 1970s.   The second set will recapture the electricity of the 1990
 s era by focusing on songs from the Allman Brothers’ renaissance. In cel
 ebrating this 10th year\, this will be a concert for the ages\, with a lin
 eup featuring The Allman Betts Band\, Robert Randolph\, Judith Hill\, Andy
  Frasco\, Luther Dickinson\, Jimmy Hall\, Steel Beans\, Larry McCray\, Cod
 y Dickinson\, Alex Orbison\, and Abby Stachschmidt**.\n**Lineup subject to
  change without notice.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261029
LOCATION:200 Maple Leaf Boulevard\, Nashville\, IN 47448
ORGANIZER;CN="Brown County Music Center":MAILTO:boxoffice@browncountymusic
 center.com
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://browncounty.com/events/the-allman-betts-family-revival/
X-SOURCE:Brown County Events
END:VEVENT
