SUMMARY:Full Moon Hike Series
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261125T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261125T213000
DTSTAMP:20260630T150125Z
UID:MEC-d6df48fe62ebe5e6a2203c5521c26dd7@browncounty.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261125T190000
SEQUENCE:4
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://browncounty.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/
 06/Untitled-design-36.jpg
CATEGORIES:Family Friendly,Free,Happening,Outdoor Adventure,Tours
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260630
DESCRIPTION:Things to know for night hikes: wear close toed shoes (not san
 dals) and dress for the weather. Red lights are preferred for night vision
  and can be loaned to hikers if necessary. Please do not bring pets on nig
 ht hikes. Hikers must stay with the group on night hikes.\nOgle Lake hikes
  use Trail 7 and are considered very rugged in the dark. Salt Creek Trail 
 Hikes are considered moderate in the dark. Meet at the Olympic Pool for Sa
 lt Creek Hikes.\nFor questions and detailed hike information\, visit the N
 ature Center\, call 812-988-5240\, email the natralist at emajor@dnr.in.go
 v or visit on in.gov/BrownCountySP\nSchedule:\n\nJanuary 3rd\, 7pm\, Ogle 
 Lake\nJanuary 31st\, 7pm\, Salt Creek Trail\nFebruary 28th\, 7pm\, Salt Cr
 eek Trail\nApril 3rd\, 8:30\, Ogle Lake\nMay 1st\, 9pm\, Ogle Lake\nMay 30
 th\, 9pm Salt Creek Trail\nJun 27th\, 9:30pm Salt Creek Trail\nJuly 31st\,
  9:30pm Ogle Lake\nAugust 28th\, 8:30pm Ogle Lake\nSeptember 26th\, 7:30pm
  Salt Creek Trail\nOctober 24th\, 7pm Salt Creek Trail\nDecember 23rd\, 7p
 m Salt Creek Trail\n\n \n
LAST-MODIFIED:20260724
LOCATION:Brown County State Park
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://browncounty.com/events/full-moon-hike-series/
X-SOURCE:Brown County Events
END:VEVENT
