 the academic year. During the summer\, testing is available on the <strong
 >first and third Thursdays</strong> of each month.</p><p>  In addition\, d
 uring the academic year\, the <strong>Monroe County Health Department</str
 ong> offers <strong>free chlamydia and gonorrhea testing</strong> on the <
 strong>third Thursday of every month</strong>\, also from <strong>10:00 a.
 m. to 1:00 p.m.</strong> in Room 101.</p><p>  The LGBTQ+ Culture Center al
 so offers a variety of <strong>free safer sex supplies</strong>\, includin
 g condoms\, internal condoms\, dental dams\, lubricants\, and educational 
 materials on proper use. These resources are available to all students\, f
 ree of charge. You can find them in the kitchenette area near the back ent
 rance of the Center and are welcome to take what you need.</p><h3>  STI Te
 sting &amp\; Safer Sex Resources Beyond Campus</h3><p>  Prioritizing your 
 sexual health should be simple and accessible. In addition to services ava
 ilable at the LGBTQ+ Culture Center\, students can receive testing on camp
 us through the <span class="___xxxjie0 f1w7gpdv f1gqqdtu" data-wra="1"><a 
