DESCRIPTION:Celebrate the season and support local talent at the Tom Fidd
 lery Holiday Student Showcase! Join us at the historic Martinsville Entert
 ainment Theatre on Sunday\, November 29 at 2:00 PM for an afternoon fill
 ed with festive music and community spirit.From classic holiday carols to 
 vibrant instrumental arrangements\, students from Tom Fiddlery will take t
 he stage to share the festive pieces they’ve been mastering. It’s the 
 perfect\, family-friendly event to kick off your holiday season while chee
 ring on our rising local musicians.Date: Sunday\, November 29\, 2026Time:
  2:00 PM (Doors open at 1:00 PM)Location: Martinsville Entertainment The
 atre\, 36 E Morgan StGrab your family and friends\, grab a box of popcorn 
 at concessions\, and enjoy an heartwarming afternoon of live music right h
 ere in downtown Martinsville!Doors open one hour before shows for ticket a
 nd concession sales. ACCESSIBILITY INFORMATIONWhen selecting your seats fo
 r non-general admission shows\, please be aware that balcony access is via
  stairs only. Wheelchair-accessible seating is available for guests who us
 e wheelchairs. There is no seat in wheelchair-accessible seating.CONCESSIO
 NS ARE AVAILABLEPlease do not bring any outside food\, beverages or drink 
 containers. Concessions open one hour before the start of every show.WHAT 
 IS YOUR REFUND POLICY?All sales are final. We do not offer exchanges for o
 ther movies or performances. Tickets can be forwarded to friends and famil
 y.WILL THE MET CANCEL SHOWS FOR BAD WEATHER?In the interest of public safe
 ty\, shows may be postponed. Every effort will be made to reschedule inste
 ad of cancel.HOW CAN I PAY FOR MY TICKETS AND CONCESSIONS?The MET now acce
 pts cash\, debit or credit cards for your convenience. Box Office opens on
 e hour before shows for in-person sales. 
