ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/11/width/168/height/168/crop/1
 /src_region/0,0,768,768/33032_2-thumbnail-WEB.rev.1791831052.jpg
CATEGORIES:Lectures, talks, seminars, and conferences
DESCRIPTION:Today's 60-minute Virtual Information Session will offer guida
 nce on crafting your application and an opportunity to interact with and p
 ose questions to Miller Program Director Daniel Martinez.  The J. Irwin Mi
 ller Master of Architecture program is a three-year in-residence program\,
  with a two-year advanced placement track possible for students who hold a
  B.Arch from a NAAB-accredited institution or regional equivalent. With ou
 r twin studios approach\, students take visual art course alongside archit
 ectural studios to develop their style of architectural design. The three-
 year program welcome applicants from a variety of educational and career b
 ackgrounds.
LAST-MODIFIED:20261012T185308Z
LOCATION:Virtual
URL:https://events.iu.edu/soaadiub/event/2447912-miller-architecture-progr
 am-virtual-info-session-cra
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p class="p1">  Today's 60-minute Virtual Inf
 ormation Session will offer guidance on crafting your application and an o
 pportunity to interact with and pose questions to Miller Program Director 
 Daniel Martinez.</p><p class="p1">  The J. Irwin Miller Master of Architec
 ture program is a three-year in-residence program\, with a two-year advanc
 ed placement track possible for students who hold a B.Arch from a NAAB-acc
 redited institution or regional equivalent. With our twin studios approach
 \, students take visual art course alongside architectural studios to deve
 lop their style of architectural design. The three-year program welcome ap
 plicants from a variety of educational and career backgrounds.</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-CONTACT-INFO:<p class="p1">\n  Yaël Ksander<br />\n  Director
  of Communications and Marketing<br />\n  Eskenazi School of Art\, Archite
 cture + Design<br />\n  <a href="mailto:yksander@iu.edu">yksander@iu.edu</
 a>\n</p>
