BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events Livewhale 237": "https://events.iu.edu/lgbtq/event/2376644-hivsti-testing"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_237
SUMMARY:HIV/STI Testing
DTSTART:20261203T150000Z
DTEND:20261203T180000Z
DTSTAMP:20260810T150649Z
UID:20261105T150000Z-2376644@events.iu.edu__20261203
DESCRIPTION:Free HIV Testing &amp\; Safer Sex Supplies at the LGBTQ+ Cultu
 re Center  Taking care of your sexual health is an important part of your 
 overall well-being\, and we're committed to making resources accessible\, 
 welcoming\, and judgment-free.Positive Link (https://iuhealth.org/find-med
 ical-services/positive-link-hiv-services) provides free and confidential H
 IV testing in Room 204 of the LGBTQ+ Culture Center every Thursday from 10
 :00 a.m. to 1:00 p.m. during the academic year. During the summer\, testin
 g is available on the first and third Thursdays of each month.  In additio
 n\, during the academic year\, the Monroe County Health Department offers 
 free chlamydia and gonorrhea testing on the third Thursday of every month
 \, also from 10:00 a.m. to 1:00 p.m. in Room 101.  The LGBTQ+ Culture Cent
 er also offers a variety of free safer sex supplies\, including condoms\, 
 internal condoms\, dental dams\, lubricants\, and educational materials on
  proper use. These resources are available to all students\, free of charg
 e. You can find them in the kitchenette area near the back entrance of the
  Center and are welcome to take what you need.  STI Testing &amp\; Safer S
 ex Resources Beyond Campus  Prioritizing your sexual health should be simp
 le and accessible. In addition to services available at the LGBTQ+ Culture
  Center\, students can receive testing on campus through the IU Student He
 alth Center (https://healthcenter.indiana.edu/medical/sti-testing/index.ht
 ml) or visit several local organizations (https://healthcenter.indiana.edu
 /health-answers/sexual-health/sti-testing-resources.html) that offer free 
 or low-cost testing and prevention services.  Many of these providers offe
 r confidential care\, safer sex supplies\, and supportive information abou
 t prevention\, treatment\, and sexual wellness. If you're unsure where to 
 start\, we're happy to help connect you with resources that fit your needs
 .All Indiana University events\, groups\, activities\, educational\, cultu
 ral\, and historical observances welcome all members of the Indiana Univer
 sity community.
GEO:39.168722;-86.525274
LAST-MODIFIED:20261027T152557Z
LOCATION:LGBTQ+ CULTURE CENTER
URL:https://events.iu.edu/lgbtq/event/2376644-hivsti-testing
