DESCRIPTION:This film explores the transformative power of creative resolv
 e in global health. From the frontlines of Rwanda's HIV fight to the histo
 ric eradication of smallpox\, it goes behind the scenes with the activists
  and experts who refused to accept the status quo. It's more than a histor
 y of medicine\; it's a blueprint for a future where health is a right\, no
 t a privilege\, and international solidarity is our strongest vaccine.  &#
 160\;Screening followed by a panel discussion and Q&amp\;A:  &#160\;Nicole
  Hassoun  Professor\, Department of International Studies  Hamilton Lugar 
 School of Global and International Studies  Director\, Global Health Impac
 t Project  &#160\;Molly Rosenberg  Professor\, Department of Epidemiology 
 and Biostatistics  IU School of Public Health\, Bloomington  &#160\;Julia 
 Sherry (Moderator)  Lecturer\, Department of Applied Health Science  Direc
 tor\, Global Health  IU School of Public Health\, Bloomington
