 1/src_region/0,0,3200,2120/32920_Snowy_Wylie_Feb_2021_00.rev.1791316059.jp
 g
CATEGORIES:Art and museum exhibitions,Community events
DESCRIPTION:The historic 1835 home is adorned with fresh greenery and seas
 onal décor\, while tours bring Wylie family stories and holiday tradition
 s to life.  Tours begin at the top of each hour\, with the final tour begi
 nning at 3 p.m.  No registration is needed\, but we ask that groups of 8 o
 r more contact us in advance at libwylie@iu.edu (mailto:libwylie@iu.edu) o
 r (812) 855-6224.Parking: Designated\, free Wylie House parking spots are 
 located behind the museum and education center\, accessible via the alley.
  Free street parking is located directly in front of the museum on 2nd St.
 Accessibility: The museum has accessible parking next to the museum's Mort
 on C. Bradley\, Jr. Education Center\, with a path that leads to a ramp at
  the back door entrance of the museum. While the historic home's second fl
 oor is only accessible by staircase\, digital images and virtual tour opti
 ons are provided for visitors who cannot visit the second floor. Please co
 ntact us in advance of your visit to discuss any specific needs.
GEO:39.161697;-86.5309
LAST-MODIFIED:20261007T164200Z
LOCATION:WYLIE HOUSE (307 E. SECOND STREET)
URL:https://events.iu.edu/libraries/event/2441814-winter-holiday-tours-at-
 wylie-house-museum
