 ang="EN-US" xml:lang="EN-US" data-contrast="auto"><span class="NormalTextR
 un SCXW253058102 BCX4">The historic 1835 home is adorned with fresh greene
 ry and seasonal décor\, while tours bring Wylie family stories and holida
 y traditions to life.</span></span></p><p>  Tours begin at the top of each
  hour\, with the final tour beginning at 3 p.m.</p><p>  No registration is
  needed\, but we ask that groups of 8 or more contact us in advance at <a 
 href="mailto:libwylie@iu.edu">libwylie@iu.edu</a> or (812) 855-6224.</p><p
 ><strong>Parking:</strong> Designated\, free Wylie House parking spots are
  located behind the museum and education center\, accessible via the alley
 . Free street parking is located directly in front of the museum on 2nd St
 .</p><p><strong>Accessibility:</strong> The museum has accessible parking 
 next to the museum's Morton C. Bradley\, Jr. Education Center\, with a pat
 h that leads to a ramp at the back door entrance of the museum. While the 
 historic home's second floor is only accessible by staircase\, digital ima
 ges and virtual tour options are provided for visitors who cannot visit th
 e second floor. Please contact us in advance of your visit to discuss any 
 specific needs.</p>
