BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Comedy Attic": "https://www.comedyattic.com/shows/375359"}
X-SOURCE-ID:comedy_attic
SUMMARY:Denny Love: Show Love Tour
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261204T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261204T210000
UID:20261204-denny-love-show-love-tour-1900
DESCRIPTION:Introducing Denny Love\, a Los Angeles–based actor and comed
 ian whose career seamlessly bridges prestige television\, live comedy\, an
 d viral digital culture. A celebrated alumnus of DePaul University’s ren
 owned Theatre School\, Denny first broke through with a standout performan
 ce in Hulu’s Looking for Alaska\, a critically acclaimed series boasting
  a 92% Rotten Tomatoes rating. He went on to appear in two seasons of Tayl
 or Sheridan’s hit Paramount+ drama Mayor of Kingstown\, further solidify
 ing his dramatic range. Beyond the screen\, Denny is a commanding live per
 former who has shared stages with comedy heavyweights like Chris D’Elia 
 and delivered memorable sets opening for Theo Von. As a key cast member of
  @KevinLangue’s viral YouTube and TikTok content\, he has helped build a
  digital powerhouse of over 4.47 million subscribers and more than 2 billi
 on views worldwide. Denny Love’s live stand up presence is rapidly becom
 ing one of the most exciting forces in comedy. He’s been taking the come
 dy scene by storm by performing at the most coveted venues in and around t
 he LA area\, across the country and internationally. Most notably\; The La
 ugh Factory\, The Comedy Store\, Improv\, Haha Comedy Club\, Comedy Chatea
 u\, Jam in the Van\, Don’t Tell Comedy\, Can’t Even\, and many more. H
 e recently headlined at the Tokyo Comedy Bar in Tokyo\, Japan and ROR Come
 dy Club in Osaka\, Japan. Denny was seen on stages all across America and 
 Canada while on tour with Chris D’elia and most recently in Las Vegas wi
 th Theo Von. In 2026\, he takes the stage at Netflix Is a Joke\, solidifyi
 ng his place among the most sought-after rising voices in entertainment. T
 his summer\, he joins the Kevin Langue Show as a key performer on an ambit
 ious 18- city national theatre tour\, bringing his sharp timing and undeni
 able charisma to audiences across the country. Building on that momentum\,
  Denny will launch his first headlining tour in Fall 2026\, marking a majo
 r milestone as he steps fully into his own spotlight.
LOCATION:The Comedy Attic\, 123 S Walnut Street\, Bloomington\, IN
URL:https://www.comedyattic.com/shows/375359
X-SOURCE:The Comedy Attic
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events Livewhale 11": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2464836-happyapero"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_11
SUMMARY:HappyApero
DTSTART:20261204T190000Z
DTEND:20261204T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20261030T165329Z
UID:20261204T190000Z-2468940@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20261204T190000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/234/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,3200,2400/33271_IMG_2247_3.rev.1793109680.jpg
CATEGORIES:Health and wellness,Lectures, talks, seminars, and conferences
DESCRIPTION:Please join us for an afternoon of discussion surrounding digi
 tal media\, online identity\, and mental health alongside our ongoing Happ
 iness 2.0 Project. An introduction will be led by Eskenazi Museum's Wilma 
 E. Kelley Director Mindy Besaw\, highlighting the importance of integratin
 g arts and sciences\, followed by a further presentation from the Happines
 s 2.0 Team. Anyone interested is welcome to attend.  The Happiness 2.0 Pro
 ject is a collaboration of the Eskenazi Museum of Art\, The Media School\,
  and IU Counseling and Psychological Services. More information about this
  initiative can be found on the Happiness 2.0 web page. (https://mediascho
 ol.indiana.edu/research/happiness-2.html)
GEO:39.169144;-86.519739
LAST-MODIFIED:20261030T205329Z
LOCATION:SIDNEY AND LOIS ESKENAZI MUSEUM OF ART
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2464836-happyapero
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Please join us for an afternoon of discu
 ssion surrounding digital media\, online identity\, and mental health alon
 gside our ongoing Happiness 2.0 Project. An introduction will be led by Es
 kenazi Museum's Wilma E. Kelley Director Mindy Besaw\, highlighting the im
 portance of integrating arts and sciences\, followed by a further presenta
 tion from the Happiness 2.0 Team. Anyone interested is welcome to attend.<
 /p><p>  The Happiness 2.0 Project is a collaboration of the Eskenazi Museu
 m of Art\, The Media School\, and IU Counseling and Psychological Services
 . More information about this initiative can be found on the <a href="http
 s://mediaschool.indiana.edu/research/happiness-2.html">Happiness 2.0 web p
 age.</a></p>
X-LIVEWHALE-CONTACT-INFO:<div id="lw_cal_event_detail_contact" class="lw_c
 al_event_detail_block mt-default">\n  <div>\n    <div>\n      <strong>Keat
