DTSTART:20261208T150000Z
DTEND:20261208T160000Z
LOCATION:IU Museum of Archaeology and Anthropology\, 416 N. Indiana Ave.\
 , Bloomington\, IN 47408
GEO:39.170023;-86.526132
SUMMARY:Community Flow with Vibe Yoga - December
DESCRIPTION:Start your morning with a relaxing yoga class. This program w
 ill be recurring monthly throughout the fall semester.Event Details:    J
 oin Vibe Yoga at the IU Museum of Archaeology and Anthropology for a free
 -to-attend flow to connect with the community and find a space that feels
  grounded\, safe\, and gently energizing. This class is beginner friendly
  and welcomes all experience levels.      These classes are designed arou
 nd vinyasa\, seamlessly moving form pose into the next. Often referred to
  as a moving meditation\, vinyasa means to "place in a special way." The 
 practice helps us flow toward our most vibrant life.  Pre-registration is
  required at vibeyogastudio.com (http://vibeyogastudio.com)    Located at
  the IU Museum of Archaeology and Anthropology    Virgil T. Devault Progr
 ams Room (Room 111)    416 N Indiana Ave\, Bloomington\, IN 47408      Th
 is class will occur monthly at 10am on:    Tuesday\, September 29    Tues
 day\, October 13    Tuesday\, November 10    Tuesday\, December 8  Parkin
 g Information:  Limited complimentary parking is available in front of th
 e Museum entrance (https://maps.app.goo.gl/k4Txsojst2gSW5fUA) off Indiana
  Avenue. Street parking is free on weekdays after 5:00 PM in the neighbor
 hoods surrounding the Museum. Paid parking options include the University
  Collections at McCalla (https://maps.app.goo.gl/3i62KNcjDeCACruHA) parki
 ng lot off Indiana Avenue\, the Indiana Memorial Union (https://maps.app.
 goo.gl/2n49VoLuF78o5twJA) visitor lot\, and nearby metered street parking
 .  Convenient metered street parking is available in the downtown/Sample 
 Gates area along Kirkwood Avenue\, East 6th Street\, East 4th Street\, No
 rth Lincoln Street\, North Dunn Street\, and South Grant Street.Questions
 ?  For accessibility assistance or questions about this event\, please re
 ach out to Camden Hill at camrhill@iu.edu (mailto:camrhill@iu.edu) or (81
 2) 855-1696.Note:  By attending this event\, you agree to be in photograp
 hy that may be used by the University for promotional purposes. If you wo
 uld not like to be in any pictures\, please speak to a Museum staff membe
 r and they will inform assigned photographers of your request. If you see
  that your image has been used in error\, please reach out to iumaa@iu.ed
 u (mailto:iumaa@iu.edu) to request that it be taken down.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Start your morning with a relaxing yoga
  class. This program will be recurring monthly throughout the fall semest
 er.</p><p><strong>Event Details:</strong></p><div class="ewa-rteLine"><p>
     Join Vibe Yoga at the IU Museum of Archaeology and Anthropology for a
  free-to-attend flow to connect with the community and find a space that 
 feels grounded\, safe\, and gently energizing. This class is beginner fri
 endly and welcomes all experience levels.  </p><p>    These classes are d
 esigned around vinyasa\, seamlessly moving form pose into the next. Often
  referred to as a moving meditation\, vinyasa means to "place in a specia
 l way." The practice helps us flow toward our most vibrant life.  </p><p>
 <strong>Pre-registration is required at <a href="http://vibeyogastudio.co
 m">vibeyogastudio.com</a></strong></p><p>    Located at the IU Museum of 
 Archaeology and Anthropology<br />    Virgil T. Devault Programs Room (Ro
 om 111)<br />    416 N Indiana Ave\, Bloomington\, IN 47408  </p><p>    T
 his class will occur monthly at 10am on:<br />    Tuesday\, September 29<
 br />    Tuesday\, October 13<br />    Tuesday\, November 10<br />    Tue
 sday\, December 8  </p></div><p><strong>Parking Information:</strong></p>
 <p>  Limited complimentary parking is available in front of the <a href="
 https://maps.app.goo.gl/k4Txsojst2gSW5fUA">Museum entrance</a> off Indian
 a Avenue. Street parking is free on weekdays after 5:00 PM in the neighbo
 rhoods surrounding the Museum. Paid parking options include the <a href="
 https://maps.app.goo.gl/3i62KNcjDeCACruHA">University Collections at McCa
 lla</a> parking lot off Indiana Avenue\, the <a href="https://maps.app.go
 o.gl/2n49VoLuF78o5twJA">Indiana Memorial Union</a> visitor lot\, and near
 by metered street parking.</p><p>  Convenient metered street parking is a
 vailable in the downtown/Sample Gates area along Kirkwood Avenue\, East 6
 th Street\, East 4th Street\, North Lincoln Street\, North Dunn Street\, 
 and South Grant Street.</p><p><strong>Questions?</strong></p><p>  For acc
 essibility assistance or questions about this event\, please reach out to
  Camden Hill at <a href="mailto:camrhill@iu.edu">camrhill@iu.edu</a> or (
 812) 855-1696.</p><p><strong>Note:</strong></p><p>  By attending this eve
 nt\, you agree to be in photography that may be used by the University fo
 r promotional purposes. If you would not like to be in any pictures\, ple
 ase speak to a Museum staff member and they will inform assigned photogra
 phers of your request. If you see that your image has been used in error\
 , please reach out to <a href="mailto:iumaa@iu.edu">iumaa@iu.edu</a> to r
 equest that it be taken down.</p>
