DTEND:20261208T213000Z
DTSTAMP:20260105T151132Z
UID:20261103T200000Z-2298061@events.iu.edu__20261208
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/234/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,640,260/22832_xx2023.58_o4_1.rev.1724348809.jpg
CATEGORIES:Art and museum exhibitions,Culture and languages,Health and wel
 lness
DESCRIPTION:Looking for a welcoming space to crochet\, knit\, embroider\, 
 quilt\, and explore other fiber arts? Interested in sharing your experienc
 es and connecting with others while learning new skills? Or even just want
  a place to vent while you work on your scarf you've been crocheting for 2
  years? Look no further\; join us for Common Threads!  Common Threads is a
  free program open to the public and offers a welcoming environment to sha
 re\, unwind\, and learn! You can bring your own fiber art to work on while
  working alongside others who enjoy working in fiber and textiles. Or you 
 can try learning something new\; we welcome all skill levels! Either way\,
  you're sure to have a good time.  This group meets on the 1st and 3rd Tue
 sday of each month from 3–4:30 p.m.\, excluding holidays and museum clos
 ures. The group will meet in the Roehm Family Art-making Studio\, located 
 inside the Simpson Center for Education on the 2nd floor of the Eskenazi M
 useum of Art.
GEO:39.169144;-86.519739
LAST-MODIFIED:20261012T182930Z
LOCATION:SIDNEY AND LOIS ESKENAZI MUSEUM OF ART
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2154813-common-threads
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Looking for a welcoming space to crochet
 \, knit\, embroider\, quilt\, and explore other fiber arts? Interested in 
 sharing your experiences and connecting with others while learning new ski
 lls? Or even just want a place to vent while you work on your scarf you've
  been crocheting for 2 years? Look no further\; join us for Common Threads
 !</p><p>  Common Threads is a free program open to the public and offers a
  welcoming environment to share\, unwind\, and learn! You can bring your o
 wn fiber art to work on while working alongside others who enjoy working i
 n fiber and textiles. Or you can try learning something new\; we welcome a
 ll skill levels! Either way\, you're sure to have a good time.</p><p>  Thi
 s group meets on the 1st and 3rd Tuesday of each month from 34:30 p.m.\, e
 xcluding holidays and museum closures. The group will meet in the Roehm Fa
 mily Art-making Studio\, located inside the Simpson Center for Education o
 n the 2nd floor of the Eskenazi Museum of Art.</p>
