X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events Livewhale 11": "https://events.iu.edu/soaadiub/event/2435603-daniel-luis-martinez-the-blueprint-exhibition"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_11
SUMMARY:Daniel Luis Martinez: The Blueprint | Exhibition
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261211
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261212
DTSTAMP:20260930T094548Z
UID:20261211T050000Z-2435603@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID;VALUE=DATE:20261211
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/11/width/168/height/168/crop/1
 /src_region/0,0,768,768/32784_260911_CAMi_Promotional_Image_05-detail-WEB.
 rev.1790774789.jpg
CATEGORIES:Art and museum exhibitions
DESCRIPTION:Opening reception: Friday\, October 2\, 2026\, 6–10pm  Exhib
 ition on view: October 2–December 18\, 2026  For this exhibition\, the b
 lueprint is used as both a representational and conceptual departure point
 . Daniel Luis Martinez uses cyanotype printmaking and mixed-media drawing 
 techniques as a generative process to imagine a speculative home on the CA
 Mi campus. The hybrid drawings and prints featured in the exhibition explo
 re the tactile middle-ground of the blueprint as a creative endeavor.  The
  series employs orthographic conventions typical of architectural drawing 
 sets\, though not as precise instructions for building. Rather\, a layered
  and loose approach expresses ideas of home as an architectonic language. 
  Daniel Luis Martinez is a registered architect\, educator\, and co-founde
 r of the multi-disciplinary design studio LAA Office\, which explores the 
 intersection of landscape\, art\, and architecture. His research and creat
 ive work investigate the potential of public art to generate alternative f
 orms of placemaking. Martinez is Associate Professor and Director of the I
 U Eskenazi School's J. Irwin Miller Architecture Program (https://architec
 ture.indiana.edu/index.html) in Columbus\, Indiana.  Learn more about the 
 exhibition at the CAMI website (https://camindy.org/exhibitions-all/theblu
 eprint).
GEO:39.72915;-86.138756
LAST-MODIFIED:20260930T134621Z
LOCATION:The Contemporary Art Museum of Indianapolis
URL:https://events.iu.edu/soaadiub/event/2435603-daniel-luis-martinez-the-
 blueprint-exhibition
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><strong>Opening reception: Friday\, Octobe
 r 2\, 2026\, 6–10pm<br />  Exhibition on view</strong>: October 2–Dece
 mber 18\, 2026</p><p>  For this exhibition\, the blueprint is used as both
  a representational and conceptual departure point. Daniel Luis Martinez u
 ses cyanotype printmaking and mixed-media drawing techniques as a generati
 ve process to imagine a speculative home on the CAMi campus. The hybrid dr
 awings and prints featured in the exhibition explore the tactile middle-gr
 ound of the blueprint as a creative endeavor.</p><p>  The series employs o
 rthographic conventions typical of architectural drawing sets\, though not
  as precise instructions for building. Rather\, a layered and loose approa
 ch expresses ideas of home as an architectonic language.</p><p>  Daniel Lu
 is Martinez is a registered architect\, educator\, and co-founder of the m
 ulti-disciplinary design studio LAA Office\, which explores the intersecti
 on of landscape\, art\, and architecture. His research and creative work i
 nvestigate the potential of public art to generate alternative forms of pl
 acemaking. Martinez is Associate Professor and Director of the IU Eskenazi
  School's <a class="external" href="https://architecture.indiana.edu/index
 .html">J. Irwin Miller Architecture Program</a> in Columbus\, Indiana.</p>
 <p>  Learn more about the exhibition at the <a class="external" href="http
 s://camindy.org/exhibitions-all/theblueprint">CAMI website</a>.</p>
