SUMMARY:Mark O’Connor’s An Appalachian Christmas
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261213T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261213T190000
DTSTAMP:20260730T133151Z
UID:MEC-863f1398173973f4eca54015e39ff8ef@browncounty.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261213T190000
SEQUENCE:1
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://browncounty.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/
 06/2-scaled.jpeg
CATEGORIES:Entertainment,Family Friendly,Happening,Holiday,Live Music,Thea
 tre &amp\; Entertainment
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260730
DESCRIPTION:Grammy-winning composer and fiddler Mark O’Connor will bring
  An Appalachian Christmas Featuring Maggie O’Connor to Nashville\, Ind.
 \, this holiday season\, with a stop at the Brown County Music Center on S
 unday\, December 13\, 2026.\nMark O’Connor’s An Appalachian Christmas 
 album (2011) reached the #1 ranking on Billboard’s Bluegrass Album chart
 s. Hailed by critics from the Wall Street Journal\, New York Times and Los
  Angeles Times as a top 10 album of the holiday season\, it has become a p
 erennial classic Christmas recording. For this concert tour\, Mark O’Con
 nor has created several arrangements of Christmas classics and a wondrous 
 mixture of both instrumental and vocal music in bluegrass and other Americ
 an music genres. Concertgoers are treated to fresh takes on traditional so
 ngs with a few original compositions included. His renditions are playful 
 and joyous\, but can be strikingly earnest too. Mark O’Connor’s Christ
 mas concerts feature himself performing on four instruments\; fiddle\, aco
 ustic guitar\, mandolin and mandocello\, with his wife and fellow Grammy- 
 winner Maggie O’Connor on fiddle and vocals. Mark and Maggie have perfor
 med An Appalachian Christmas together as husband and wife for nearly 10 ye
 ars\, and together they’ve captured it all on their most recent album A 
 Christmas Duo. Much of the year they tour behind their latest recording of
  original Americana songs and classics\, Life After Life. Together on stag
 e\, Mark and Maggie have a dynamic energy that bring their individual expe
 rtise to holiday themes and classics in the most delightful and musically 
 satisfying way!\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20260730
LOCATION:200 Maple Leaf Boulevard\, Nashville\, IN 47448
ORGANIZER;CN="Brown County Music Center":MAILTO:boxoffice@browncountymusic
 center.com
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://browncounty.com/events/mark-oconnors-an-appalachian-christmas/
X-SOURCE:Brown County Events
END:VEVENT
